   - Increased production of pro-inflammatory cytokines (e.g., IL-6, IL-1β) in the early stages of stress, which can indirectly impair NK cell function.
   - Altered cytokine production by other immune cells, such as T cells and B cells, which can indirectly impact NK cell function.

