","To find the maximum height reached by the particle, we can use the kinematic equations for constant acceleration. The initial velocity is \(v_0 = 20 \, \text{m/s}\), the acceleration is \(a = -9.8 \, \text{m/s}^2\) (downward), and the final velocity at the maximum height is \(v = 0 \, \text{m/s}\).

