   - When oxygen binds, it replaces the water molecule in the empty coordination site, forming a new coordination complex (Fe²⁺ → Fe²⁺-O₂).
   - The oxygen ion binds in a square-tetranedral manner, with the Fe²⁺ ion at the center and the oxygen ligand at one of the four coordination sites.

