At the maximum height, \( v = 0 \), so:
\[ 0 = 20^2 + (-9.8)(2y) \]
\[ 0 = 400 - 19.8y \]
\[ 19.8y = 400 \]
\[ y = \frac{400}{19.8} \approx 20.00 \text{ m} \]

The difference in the two values is due to the approximation in the first method. The second method is more accurate because it does not require an intermediate step.

Thus, the maximum height reached by the particle is approximately \( 20.00 \, \text{m} \).

