2. **Functional isomerism**: This occurs when isomers have the same molecular formula but different functional groups (e.g., alcohol vs. aldehyde).  
3. **Stereomeric isomerism**: This occurs when isomers have the same carbon skeleton and functional groups but differ in the arrangement of atoms (e.g., cis/trans isomers or enantiomers).  

