","The joger is running at 9 km/hr and the train is running at 40 km/hr in the same direction. The distance between the joger and the engine is 150 m. The train takes 22 seconds to pass the joger.
First, convert the speeds to m/s:
Joger's speed = 9 km/hr = 9 * (1000 m) / (1000 s) = 9 m/s.
Train's speed = 45 km/hr = 45 * (1000 m) / (1000 s) = 45 m/s.
The relative speed of the train with respect to the joger is the difference in their speeds, since they are moving in the same direction:
Relative speed = 45 m/s - 9 m/s = 36 m/s.
The time taken for the train to pass the joger is 25 seconds.
During this time, the train must cover the distance of 150 m (the distance between the joger and the engine) plus the length of the train.
The distance covered by the train relative to the jogjer is the relative speed multiplied by the time taken:
