\]

Now, we can use the diffraction grating formula to find the angle \(\theta\) for the third order maximum (\(n = 3\)):
\[
d \sin \theta = n \lambda
\]
\[
1.0 \times 10^{-3} \, \text{m} \sin \theta = 3 \times 600 \times 10^{-18} \, \text{m}
\]
\[
1.0 \times 10^{-3} \, \text{m} \sin \theta = 1.8 \times 10^{-16} \, \text{m}
\]
\[
\sin \theta = \frac{1.8 \times 10^{-16} \, \text{m}}{1.0 \times 10^{-3} \, \text{m}} = 1.8 \times 10^{-13}
\]
\[
\theta = \sin^{-1}(1.8 \times 10^{-13})
\]
