Given:  
\[ m = 30 \, \text{kg} \)  
\[ F = 32 \, \text{N} \)  
Substituting the given values into the formula:  
\[ a = \frac{32 \, \text{N}}{30 \, \text{kg}} = 1.06 \, \text{m/s}^2 \]  
The acceleration of the particle is \(\boxed{1.06 \, \text{m/s}^2}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

