- Initial volume \( V_1 = 4 \, \text{L} \)
- Final volume \( V_2 = 8 \, \text{L} \)

Since the gas is expanding isothermically, the pressure changes proportionally to the inverse of the volume:
\[
P_1 V_1 = P_2 V_2
\]
Substituting the given values:
\[
2 \, \text{atm} \times 4 \, \text{L} = P_2 \times 8 \, \text{L}
\]
Solving for \( P_2 \):
\[
P_2 = \frac{2 \times 4}{8} = 1 \, \text{atm}
\]

