","The energy transferred by friction friction is converted into heat, which raises the temperature of the hands and the surrounding environment. The friction force is proportional to the mean relative velocity of the hands, and the energy transferred per unit time is the power done by the friction force. The power is:
\[ P = F_{\text{fr}} v \)
This power is converted into heat, and the heat supplied to the hands and the environment is:
\[ Q = P = F_{\text{fr}} v \, \Delta t = \Delta Q_{\text{hands}} + \Delta Q_{\text{environment}} \]
