\[

\lambda = \frac{1.1 \times 10^12}{E_o \text{ (keV})} \left( \frac{E_o}{E_p} \right) \left ( \frac{E_o}{E_o + E_p} \right)^ 2 \text{ cm}^2
\]  
where \( e^{-1} \) is the electron energy in keV and \( \lambda \) is the cross section in cm\(^2\).  

This formula is valid for low-energy electrons (\( E_o \)) and is empirically derived.  

