","The derivation of the stability of the Duffort-Frankel method involves the following steps:

1. **Transform the equation to the form of a first-order equation**:  
   The Duffort-Frankel equation is a first-order solution for \( \phi_{j}^{n+1} \).  
   \[
   \phi_{j}^{n+1} + \frac{\partial \phi}{\partial t} = \phi_{j}^{n-1} + \frac{2\kappa \Delta t}{(\Delta x)^2} \left \left(\phi_{j+1}^n - \phi_{j}^n - \phi_{j}^{n-1} + \phi_{j-1}^n \right)
   \]
   Substituting \(\phi_{j}^{n+1} = \phi_{j}^{n} + \Delta dt \left( \frac{\partial \phi}{\partial t} \right) = \phi_{j}^{n} + \Delta dt \cdot \frac{\partial \phi}{\partial t}\), and \(\phi_{j}^{n-1} = \phi_{j}^{n} - \Delta dt \left \(\frac{\partial \phi}{\partial t} \right\), we have:
   \[
   \phi_{j}^{n} + \Delta dt \left \(\frac{\partial \phi}{\partial t} \right) = \phi_{j}^{n} - \Delta dt \left \(\frac{\partial \phi}{\partial t} \right) + \frac{2\kappa \Delta t}{(\Delta x)^2} \left \(\phi_{j+1} - \phi_{j} - \phi_{j-1} + \phi_{j+1} \right)
   \]
